@@ -309,6 +309,12 @@ again.
   terminal navigation actions. The right pane keeps the chat prompt visible while scroll offsets
   reveal earlier transcript rows.
 
+In command mode, `TerminalUi` supports character, line, and block visual selections in the focused
+pane. `v`, `V`, and `Ctrl-V` select text from the rendered left or right pane; `h`, `j`, `k`, `l`,
+and arrow keys move the selection cursor; `y` copies the selected text and `Y` copies linewise text.
+Copying emits an OSC52 clipboard sequence at the start of the next render frame and then clears the
+selection.
+
 `src/ui_harness.rs::UiHarness` is the test harness for terminal behavior. It exercises the same
 `TerminalUi` frame path used by the interactive example. UI tests should drive
 `UiHarness::handle_byte` or `UiHarness::handle_bytes` rather than duplicating terminal input logic.
